<%# HALF TWO: WHAT THE PHOTOGRAPHS PRODUCED.

    TWO WAYS TO A PICTURE, and they are alternatives rather than stages.

    ZERO-SHOT (top) hands a generator ONE headshot at generation time and gets an
    image back. No training step, so no preparation stage to fail.

    TRAINED (bottom) asks Higgsfield to build a persistent character identity from
    a photo set first. Stronger when it works, and four of six measured attempts
    refused the photo set outright.

    THE PICTURES LEAD, because the operator's question about this page is "can I
    see the thing we made". The controls sit under them and the trained identity,
    which is a status rather than a picture, sits at the bottom.

    THE VENDOR RE-HOSTS OUR REFERENCE PHOTOS on their CDN and showing those would
    look more impressive here, but they are their copies of our INPUT, and
    labelling input as output is exactly the muddle this page exists to clear up. %>
<% chip = identity_chip(@appearance) %>

<div data-test="model-output-panel" class="card p-4 sm:p-5 space-y-5">
  <header class="space-y-1">
    <p class="label-upper text-primary">2 &middot; Output</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Character sheets</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted">
      Made from the photographs on the left. Every image records which generator
      produced it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <%# THE GALLERY. One image renders full width rather than in a two-up grid: the
      spike buys exactly one, and the question being asked of it is "is this
      recognisably him", which a half-width thumbnail cannot answer.

      object-contain, NOT object-cover. A crop that trims the head or the feet
      destroys the one thing a full-body test is looking for. Letterboxing against
      the inset background is the honest rendering. %>
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <% if @artifacts.any? %>
      <%# ALWAYS ONE COLUMN. A ten-panel sheet at half the width of a narrow
          column is unreadable, and the question asked of it — is every panel the
          same man — cannot be answered from a thumbnail. %>
      <div data-test="generated-images" class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-2">
        <% @artifacts.each do |artifact| %>
          <figure class="rounded-lg border border-subtle overflow-hidden bg-surface-alt">
            <%# NO FIXED ASPECT, ON PURPOSE. This library holds two shapes that
                cannot share one box: a sheet is about 2:1 and a single portrait
                about 3:4. Any fixed ratio letterboxes one of them, and the
                wasted band is exactly the height needed to judge whether every
                panel is the same man. Natural height costs a little layout shift
                while the image loads and gives both shapes their full width. %>
            <div class="bg-inset overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center">
              <% if artifact.image_url.present? %>
                <%# LINKS OUT TO THE FULL-SIZE FILE. Judging a likeness inside a
                    narrow column is judging a thumbnail, so the picture is always
                    one click from its original. %>
                <%= link_to artifact.image_url, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                      class: "block w-full" do %>
                  <%= image_tag artifact.image_url, loading: "lazy",
                        alt: artifact.subjects.first&.role.presence || artifact.kind.to_s.humanize,
                        class: "w-full h-auto object-contain" %>
                <% end %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="text-2xl opacity-40" aria-hidden="true">&#127912;</span>
              <% end %>
            </div>

            <figcaption class="p-2 space-y-1.5">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-1 flex-wrap">
                <span class="badge text-3xs bg-surface text-muted border-subtle">
                  <%= artifact.subjects.first&.role.presence || artifact.kind.to_s.humanize %>
                </span>
                <% if artifact.approved? %>
                  <span class="badge text-3xs bg-success/10 text-success-ink border-success/40">approved</span>
                <% end %>
              </div>

              <%# THE PROVENANCE STAMP. The operator intends to swap generators as
                  capacities change, so this library will hold images from several.
                  Without the stamp a mixed library is unreadable and you cannot
                  tell a regression from a provider change.

                  An UNSTAMPED artifact says so rather than rendering blank: the
                  whole back-catalogue predates these columns, and silence there
                  reads as a bug in this caption. %>
              <% if artifact.generated? %>
                <dl data-test="artifact-provenance" class="text-3xs space-y-0.5">
                  <div class="flex gap-1">
                    <dt class="text-muted shrink-0">by</dt>
                    <dd class="text-body font-medium"><%= artifact.generator_label %></dd>
                  </div>
                  <% if artifact.generator_version.present? %>
                    <div class="flex gap-1 min-w-0">
                      <dt class="text-muted shrink-0">ver</dt>
                      <dd class="text-muted font-mono break-all"><%= artifact.generator_version %></dd>
                    </div>
                  <% end %>
                  <% if artifact.seed.present? %>
                    <div class="flex gap-1">
                      <dt class="text-muted shrink-0">seed</dt>
                      <dd class="text-muted font-mono"><%= artifact.seed %></dd>
                    </div>
                  <% end %>
                  <%# COST RENDERS ONLY WHEN THE VENDOR REPORTED IT. A blank row
                      would read as free, and free is the one thing this never is. %>
                  <%# THE UNIT IS ALWAYS NAMED. fal counts image units, OpenAI
                      counts tokens, and both land in one column, so a bare number
                      would invite comparing 3 with 18,000. A nil cost prints
                      nothing rather than zero: not reported is not free. %>
                  <% if artifact.billing_summary.present? %>
                    <div class="flex gap-1 min-w-0">
                      <dt class="text-muted shrink-0">cost</dt>
                      <dd class="text-muted font-mono break-all"><%= artifact.billing_summary %></dd>
                    </div>
                  <% end %>
                </dl>
              <% else %>
                <p class="text-3xs text-muted">Made before we recorded the generator.</p>
              <% end %>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% else %>
      <div data-test="no-generated-images"
           class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-subtle bg-surface-alt p-4 text-center space-y-1">
        <span class="text-2xl opacity-30 block" aria-hidden="true">&#127912;</span>
        <p class="text-2xs text-muted">Nothing generated yet.</p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# THE ZERO-SHOT CONTROL. Admin only, matching the controller, because it
      spends. It needs NO character model — one cached headshot is the whole
      input, which is why it renders even when the identity below reads "none". %>
  <div data-test="zero-shot-generate"
       class="rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface-alt p-3 space-y-2">
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <p class="label-upper">Generate a sheet from one photo</p>
      <% if @generator_row.present? %>
        <span class="badge text-3xs <%= @can_generate ? "bg-success/10 text-success-ink border-success/40" : "bg-surface text-muted border-subtle" %>">
          <%= @generator_row.label %>
        </span>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% if @identity_photo_url.blank? %>
      <p class="text-2xs text-warning-ink">
        No cached headshot for this person, so there is no face to build from.
      </p>
    <% elsif @generator_row.blank? %>
      <p class="text-2xs text-muted">No generator is registered for this yet.</p>
    <% elsif !@can_generate %>
      <%# NAMES THE VARIABLE. The person reading this is the person who will go
          and set it, and "not configured" without the name sends them to ask
          someone. %>
      <p class="text-2xs text-muted"><%= @generator_row.unconfigured_message %></p>
    <% elsif admin? %>
      <%= form_with url: generate_person_appearance_path(@person.slug, @appearance.slug),
                    method: :post, class: "space-y-2" do |f| %>
        <%# THE JERSEY NUMBER IS STILL TYPED, AND THAT IS NOW A CHOICE RATHER THAN A
            LIMIT. This comment used to say nothing stored a number, measured the day
            before `athletes.jersey_number` landed (Athletes::AcquireOrValidate, its
            `:roster` policy) — the column exists, and the model-pipeline card already
            prints it. What has not changed is that Appearances::CharacterSheetPrompt
            does not READ it: doing so would change the text of every generated prompt,
            and a prompt change costs money to evaluate and owes its own before/after
            artifacts, so it is a task rather than a side effect of correcting a
            comment. Until then this field is the only number the prompt sees, and left
            blank the prompt omits the number and nameplate clauses rather than asking
            the model to render a placeholder. %>
        <%= f.number_field :number, placeholder: "Jersey number (optional)",
              min: 0, max: 99, class: "input-field w-full text-xs" %>
        <%= f.submit "Generate character sheet", class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary w-full" %>
      <% end %>
      <p class="text-3xs text-muted">
        Costs money &mdash; one full sheet per press. No character model needed.
      </p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-2xs text-muted">
        <%= @generator_row.label %> is ready. Generating is an admin action.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%# THE TRAINED IDENTITY. Kept, and moved below the zero-shot path it is an
      alternative to.

      THE IDENTITY IS NOT A PICTURE, which is the honest thing this block has to
      say: its visible form is a status, an id and a count. %>
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-subtle bg-surface-alt p-3 space-y-3">
    <p class="label-upper">Trained character model</p>
    <p class="text-3xs text-muted">
      A persistent identity minted from a whole photo set. Stronger than one-photo
      generation when the set is good enough to train on.
    </p>

    <div data-test="identity-status" data-state="<%= @appearance.higgsfield_reference_state %>"
         class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <span class="badge text-3xs <%= chip[:classes] %>"><%= chip[:label] %></span>
      <% if @appearance.higgsfield_reference_status.present? %>
        <span class="text-3xs text-muted font-mono"><%= @appearance.higgsfield_reference_status %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% if @appearance.higgsfield_reference_id.present? %>
      <dl class="space-y-1.5 text-2xs">
        <div>
          <dt class="label-upper">Identity</dt>
          <%# break-all rather than truncate: this UUID is the ONLY handle that
              survives (the vendor serves no list endpoint), so it has to be
              copyable in full, and min-w-0 on the panel keeps it from widening
              the grid track. %>
          <dd class="font-mono text-heading break-all"><%= @appearance.higgsfield_reference_id %></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="label-upper">Built from</dt>
          <dd class="text-body"><%= pluralize(@identity_urls.length, "photo") %></dd>
        </div>
        <% if @appearance.higgsfield_reference_synced_at.present? %>
          <div>
            <dt class="label-upper">Last polled</dt>
            <dd class="text-body">
              <%= time_ago_in_words(@appearance.higgsfield_reference_synced_at) %> ago
            </dd>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>

      <%# A MINTED IDENTITY IS NOT USABLE UNTIL IT READS READY, and nothing moves the
          stored status on its own — the create stamps `not_ready` and only a poll
          changes it. So the poll button is the one control a pending identity needs,
          and it is free (a read). %>
      <%# ADMINS ONLY, matching the controller. The poll is free, but it is still an
          outbound call on our credential and the action refuses a non-admin, so
          offering it to the public page would be offering a redirect. %>
      <% if admin? && @appearance.higgsfield_reference_state != :ready %>
        <%= button_to "Ask Higgsfield again",
              refresh_person_appearance_path(@person.slug, @appearance.slug),
              method: :post, class: "btn btn-sm btn-neutral w-full" %>
        <p class="text-3xs text-muted">
          Free &mdash; this only reads the status. A model is unusable until it reads ready.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <p class="text-2xs text-muted">
        Nothing minted yet.
        <% if admin? %>
          Requesting one sends
          <%= pluralize(@identity_urls.length, "photo") %> to Higgsfield and costs money.
        <% end %>
      </p>
      <%# ADMINS ONLY, matching the controller. This is the most expensive button on
          the page: one identity per look, from a vendor with no list endpoint to
          recall it from. The disabled state stays for the admin who has no photos
          yet, because that is a purchase which would refuse rather than one they may
          not make. %>
      <% if admin? %>
        <%= button_to "Request the model",
              mint_person_appearance_path(@person.slug, @appearance.slug),
              method: :post,
              class: "btn btn-sm btn-neutral w-full",
              disabled: @identity_urls.empty? %>
        <% if @identity_urls.empty? %>
          <p class="text-3xs text-warning-ink">
            Needs at least one photo first.
          </p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
